<attribute name="name" nodeId="d0a3a3d7">Evaluate issue resolution alternatives</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="b3c68059">_sX0GQvyeEeOOGZZA-JKR9Q</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="26ef8f35">Evaluate issue resolution alternatives</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="ec5537fb"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="ac3429b7">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="ac629b02"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="6d565fb7">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="f6e28db0"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="303ad028">&lt;p&gt;
    If the resolution action is clear, assign the action items and close the issue. For major issues, it may be necessary
    to assign a team member to conduct an investigation to identify and list possible alternative resolutions. Always
    consider changes to the schedule, plan, and deliverables as options.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Generating alternatives is a creative process.&amp;nbsp;Be mindful that&amp;nbsp;initial brainstorming may inadvertently lock
    you into an undesirable mind-set. Document only viable alternatives. Resist the temptation to present unreasonable
    alternatives to give the illusion of choice. If there is only one viable alternative, say so.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Consider each alternative individually. Evaluate the possible impact on the project and on other projects. Develop a
    potential action plan for each alternative.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Internal impacts can occur in the following areas:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Deliverable impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Work effort impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Financial impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Schedule impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Organizational impact
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Ancillary plans&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    External impacts can include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Increasing or decreasing project credibility
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Improving or damaging user relations
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Changing the project plan or charter&lt;br /&gt;
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Based on this evaluation, rank the alternatives.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
